---
import SnippetPanel from '../../components/SnippetPanel.astro';
import Lab from '../../layouts/Lab.astro';
import { trackingSnippet } from '../../lab/tracking';
import { repoUrl } from '../../site.config';

const DOCS = 'https://docs.firework.com/firework-for-developers/web/integration-guide/shopping-integration-v2/tracking';

const events = [
  { call: 'pageViewed', request: 'user:page_viewed', when: 'Once on every page, when the shopper lands on it.', here: 'Every page.' },
  { call: 'addToCart', request: 'user:add_to_cart', when: 'Each time the store\'s cart takes an item.', here: 'Every change to the site\'s bag, from the site or from Add to Bag in a video.' },
  { call: 'removeFromCart', request: 'user:remove_from_cart', when: 'Each time an item leaves the cart.', here: 'The same, for decreases and removals. Checkout emptying the bag is not a removal.' },
  { call: 'purchase', request: 'user:purchase', when: 'On the order confirmation page, for every order.', here: 'Once per order on /order/confirmed.' },
];

// Checked against the live SDK and analytics.js (release v20261104.1) on 12 November 2026. Keep to what was observed.
const findings = [
  'The full SDK (fwn.js) contains the same analytics code as analytics.js and defines window._fwn.analytics as it loads. A page that loads fwn.js can send events without the extra tag.',
  'fwn-async.js loads the SDK only when a widget scrolls into view, or when the URL has fw_ parameters from a shared video link. A page without widgets, such as an order confirmation page, then has no window._fwn.analytics, and the purchase is never sent. That is what the analytics.js tag is for.',
  'Both scripts can be on one page. Whichever loads first defines window._fwn.analytics, and the other leaves it alone.',
  'The docs\' examples call window._fwn.analytics on DOMContentLoaded, with analytics.js loaded async. On a test page that threw "Cannot read properties of undefined" every time, fresh and cached, and nothing was sent. Wait for window._fwn.analytics instead, as in the code below.',
  'analytics.js fires fw:ready when it starts. It fires before window._fwn.shopping exists, and the SDK fires fw:ready again once shopping is ready. Shopping code that runs once on the first fw:ready never registers its hooks, and the player shows Shop Now.',
  'Each call sends a request to p2.fwpixel.com/trk/user:<event>, with the payload under event_properties.user_data. When the shopper engaged with a video, livestream or AVA chat in this browser, the request also carries their IDs, which is how a sale can be linked to a video.',
  'Add to Bag in the player sends its own commerce:click_add_to_cart, and the player\'s cart sends click_increase_in_cart, click_decrease_in_cart and click_remove_in_cart. Those are taps in the player. This site still sends addToCart and removeFromCart for those changes, with the quantity the store accepted.',
  'Not in the docs: analytics.js and the SDK can forward Google Analytics add_to_cart and purchase events from window.dataLayer to the same calls, marked source "ga_datalayer". It is off unless a Firework script tag has data-fwparam_tracking_ga_event. With it on, a store that also calls purchase() may report each order twice.',
];

const noRevenue = [
  'The sku values do not match the external IDs imported into Firework. See <a href="/learn/products-and-ids">Products and IDs</a>.',
  'The confirmation page has no window._fwn.analytics, or calls it before it loads. Look for user:purchase in the network tab after a test order.',
  'The store only sends orders that came from videos. The docs ask for every purchase, so Firework can compare shoppers who watched with those who did not.',
];
---

<Lab title="Tracking" description="Firework's tracking events on this store: the analytics script tag, page views, bag changes and purchases, with a log of what this tab sent.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Lab tool</p>
  <h1>Tracking</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The store's own pages tell Firework about page views, bag changes and orders. Firework uses them to link sales to
    videos. This site loads Firework's analytics script and sends all four events for the sandbox channel.
  </p>
  <p id="trk-status" class="note" aria-live="polite">Checking tracking…</p>

  <div class="lab-grid">
    <section aria-labelledby="trk-try-heading">
      <h2 id="trk-try-heading">Try it</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Add or remove a toner below. Each change sends <code>addToCart</code> or <code>removeFromCart</code>.</li>
        <li>Open a <a href="/products/cloudberry-vitamin-c-serum">product page</a> or a video and add something there. Its events show up here too.</li>
        <li><a href="/checkout">Check out</a>. The confirmation page sends <code>purchase</code> with the same <code>order_id</code> as the bag's events.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="trk-try">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-small" id="trk-add">Add Glacier Water Essence Toner</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-small btn-ghost" id="trk-remove">Remove one</button>
        <span id="trk-bag" class="small muted" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <aside class="panel" aria-labelledby="trk-tag-heading">
      <h2 id="trk-tag-heading">The script tag</h2>
      <p class="small">On every page that sends events, in the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>:</p>
      <pre class="trk-tag" tabindex="0"><code>&lt;script async type="text/javascript"
  src="//asset.fwcdn3.com/js/analytics.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
      <p class="small muted">
        This site adds it on every page that uses the sandbox channel, before the SDK. Nothing is added with
        <code>?fw=off</code> or on other channels.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <h2>Event log</h2>
  <p class="small muted">
    Every event this browser tab sent, newest first, from any page. Open a row to see the payload. The network tab shows
    the same calls as <code>user:*</code> requests.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="table trk-log">
      <thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>Page</th><th>Call</th><th>Result</th><th>Payload</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="trk-log"><tr><td colspan="5" class="muted">Nothing sent yet in this tab.</td></tr></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p><button type="button" class="btn btn-small btn-ghost" id="trk-clear">Clear the log</button></p>

  <h2>The four events</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="table">
      <thead><tr><th>Call</th><th>Request</th><th>When to send it</th><th>On this site</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          events.map((e) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>window._fwn.analytics.{e.call}()</code></td>
              <td><code>{e.request}</code></td>
              <td>{e.when}</td>
              <td>{e.here}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    <code>addToCart</code>, <code>removeFromCart</code> and <code>purchase</code> take the purchase format:
    <code>order_id</code>, <code>currency</code>, <code>subtotal</code>, <code>order_value</code> and
    <code>line_items</code> with <code>sku</code>, <code>quantity</code> and <code>price</code>. The docs don't say
    what a cart event's lines mean. This site sends what was added or removed, as Google Analytics does, and uses the
    bag's ID as <code>order_id</code>. That ID becomes the order ID at checkout.
  </p>

  <h2>The code</h2>
  <SnippetPanel id="trk-code" title="Tracking script" code={trackingSnippet} />
  <p class="small muted">
    This site's version is <a href={`${repoUrl}/blob/main/src/scripts/tracking.ts`}>src/scripts/tracking.ts</a>, and
    the script tag comes from <a href={`${repoUrl}/blob/main/src/scripts/firework-loader.ts`}>src/scripts/firework-loader.ts</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Checked with the live SDK</h2>
  <ul>{findings.map((f) => <li>{f}</li>)}</ul>

  <h2>"Insights shows no sales from videos"</h2>
  <p>The usual causes, most likely first:</p>
  <ol>{noRevenue.map((r) => <li set:html={r} />)}</ol>

  <h2>Docs</h2>
  <p class="small muted">
    Stores on a Firework e-commerce app (Shopify, Magento, Salesforce Commerce Cloud) don't need the purchase call: the
    app sends it.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={DOCS}>Tracking</a>, including the analytics script tag</li>
    <li><a href={`${DOCS}/purchase`}>Purchase</a>, <a href={`${DOCS}/add-to-cart`}>Add to cart</a>, <a href={`${DOCS}/remove-from-cart`}>Remove from cart</a> and <a href={`${DOCS}/page-viewed`}>Page viewed</a></li>
    <li><a href="/lab/shopping">Shopping integration</a> on this site</li>
  </ul>
</Lab>

<script>
  import { getCart, onCartChange, setLine } from '../../scripts/cart';
  import { formatEur } from '../../scripts/products-client';
  import { effectiveSettings } from '../../scripts/settings';
  import { clearTrackingLog, getTrackingLog, onTrackingLog, trackingStatus, trackRequest, type TrackingLogEntry } from '../../scripts/tracking';

  // Status: is tracking on, and did anything define window._fwn.analytics?
  const statusEl = document.getElementById('trk-status')!;
  const status = trackingStatus(effectiveSettings());
  statusEl.textContent = `${status.on ? 'On' : 'Off'}: ${status.reason}.`;
  if (status.on) {
    statusEl.classList.add('note-info');
    const started = Date.now();
    const check = () => {
      if (window._fwn?.analytics) statusEl.textContent += ' window._fwn.analytics is ready.';
      else if (Date.now() - started > 12000) statusEl.textContent += ' window._fwn.analytics did not appear within 12 seconds. Is something blocking asset.fwcdn3.com?';
      else return void window.setTimeout(check, 200);
    };
    check();
  }

  // Try it: the toner
  const TONER = { productId: 'FJB-102', unitId: 'FJB-102-200ML' };
  const bagEl = document.getElementById('trk-bag')!;
  const tonerQty = () => getCart().find((l) => l.unitId === TONER.unitId)?.quantity ?? 0;
  const showBag = () => {
    const qty = tonerQty();
    bagEl.textContent = qty ? `${qty} in the bag.` : 'None in the bag.';
    (document.getElementById('trk-remove') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = qty === 0;
  };
  document.getElementById('trk-add')!.addEventListener('click', () => setLine(TONER.productId, TONER.unitId, tonerQty() + 1));
  document.getElementById('trk-remove')!.addEventListener('click', () => setLine(TONER.productId, TONER.unitId, Math.max(0, tonerQty() - 1)));
  onCartChange(showBag);
  showBag();

  // Event log
  const logBody = document.getElementById('trk-log')!;
  const empty = logBody.innerHTML;
  const cell = (tr: HTMLTableRowElement, build: (td: HTMLTableCellElement) => void) => {
    const td = document.createElement('td');
    build(td);
    tr.appendChild(td);
  };
  const code = (text: string) => {
    const el = document.createElement('code');
    el.textContent = text;
    return el;
  };
  const summary = (e: TrackingLogEntry): string => {
    const p = e.payload as { line_items?: { sku: string; quantity: number }[]; order_value?: number } | null;
    if (e.event === 'pageViewed') return 'no customer ID';
    if (Array.isArray(p?.line_items)) return `${p.line_items.map((l) => `${l.sku} × ${l.quantity}`).join(', ')} · ${formatEur(p.order_value ?? 0)}`;
    return 'payload';
  };

  function addRow(e: TrackingLogEntry) {
    if (logBody.querySelector('td[colspan]')) logBody.replaceChildren();
    const tr = document.createElement('tr');
    if (e.status !== 'sent') tr.className = 'is-error';
    cell(tr, (td) => (td.textContent = new Date(e.at).toLocaleTimeString()));
    cell(tr, (td) => (td.textContent = e.page));
    cell(tr, (td) => {
      td.appendChild(code(e.event));
      if (e.source === 'player') {
        const badge = document.createElement('span');
        badge.className = 'badge-video';
        badge.textContent = 'from the video';
        td.append(' ', badge);
      }
    });
    cell(tr, (td) => {
      if (e.status === 'sent') td.append('Sent as ', code(trackRequest[e.event]));
      else td.textContent = `Not sent: ${e.reason}.`;
    });
    cell(tr, (td) => {
      const details = document.createElement('details');
      const sum = document.createElement('summary');
      sum.textContent = summary(e);
      const pre = document.createElement('pre');
      pre.textContent = JSON.stringify(e.payload, null, 2);
      details.append(sum, pre);
      td.appendChild(details);
    });
    logBody.prepend(tr);
  }

  getTrackingLog().forEach(addRow);
  onTrackingLog(addRow);
  document.getElementById('trk-clear')!.addEventListener('click', () => {
    clearTrackingLog();
    logBody.innerHTML = empty;
  });
</script>

<style>
  .trk-try {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .trk-tag {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  .trk-log :global(tr.is-error td) {
    color: var(--danger);
  }
  .trk-log :global(td:nth-child(2)),
  .trk-log :global(td:nth-child(4)) {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .trk-log :global(td:nth-child(4) code) {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .trk-log :global(details pre) {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
  .trk-log :global(.badge-video) {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    padding: 1px 7px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--warning-bg);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
